## Summary

**What was built**: Shared multimodal content mapping for Codex Responses API, extracted into `src/content-transform.ts` with three exports: `mapContentToCodex()`, `contentToString()`, and `looksLikeOpenAIContentArray()`. Both `src/index.ts` and `src/router.ts` updated to use the shared helper at all 6 call sites, plus `filterInput()` guard.

**Root cause**: `text: msg.content` assumed string, crashed when OpenCode sent multimodal content arrays.

**Files changed**:
- `src/content-transform.ts` — Created (shared helper + type exports)
- `src/index.ts` — Modified (imported helper, updated 3 call sites + filterInput + system extraction)
- `src/router.ts` — Modified (imported helper, updated 3 call sites + system extraction)
- `tests/unit/content-transform.test.ts` — Created (19 tests)
- `jest.config.js` — Created (ESM + ts-jest)

**Test results**: 19/19 passing, `tsc --noEmit` clean.

**Key learnings**:
- `filterInput` needed a `looksLikeOpenAIContentArray()` guard to avoid double-transforming already-Codex-formatted arrays
- Role semantics matter: `user` → `input_text`, `assistant` → `output_text`, system → string flattening
- Missing test infrastructure (jest.config.js) had to be bootstrapped

